# --- DISCOVERIES 10-24 (optional, no quest needs them): camp + note; TP_SnowVehicle01 + chest; hatch with a chest; dirt to dig (the detector comes later); viewpoint ---
place campfire_1 - at 38.3 7.4 ground sit
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_SimpleTent - at 41.3 9.4 ground sit yaw=357
place "Box Small" - at 36.3 9.9 ground sit
place Note_Paper dnote at 36.3 9.9 ground y=0.7 drop yaw=20
note dnote Sledger's note | CAMP ON THE SHELF (a note under a stone, in a round, friendly hand)\n\nTuva and Knut fed, both asleep on my feet, which is the only warm thing in the north. The ice groaned all night like an old man getting out of a chair.\nThe Kittiwake's master gave me coffee and an earful. I took their radio set "for repair" - his quotes, not mine, he did them with his fingers. They'll have it back when the Coldhold says so.\nNailed the Warden's paper up on their mast, as I was told. Halvorsen read it and spat on the deck. Good man, Halvorsen.\nThe Whale's horn sounded from the north again. No ship has a horn like that any more. Nobody says so out loud.\nOn at first light: Steamvent, then home to my goats, who have surely eaten the door.\n- O.V.
place TP_SnowVehicle01 dvan at -38.3 -7.4 ground yaw=117
prop dvan tint.color=#8a9aa6
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at -42.3 -4.4 ground sit yaw=57
note dwreckchest Frozen chest | Frozen to an old sledge runner: wool, rope, a tin of nails.
loot dwreckchest Wool*3;Rope*2;Nail*8
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=-34.1 z=18.9 r=15 seed=12291 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;Wool*3;Bolt*2
call dirt x=34.1 z=-18.9 r=15 n=3 seed=12292
place Zone_Trigger dview at -33.4 -20.1 ground
prop dview zone.id=the_floelane_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=The floes lie on the black water like broken plates, and the crushed sealing boat between them.

# --- DEEP 10-24 (one-hour pass): the floes stay the core; round them the grounded iceberg (NE, 26 m, its ice ladder to
# the sealers' lookout: the climb, the wheelhouse key froze into its top), the bear den (W, the lookout's tally), the
# sealers' hut ruin (SE), the sister boat sunk 12 m down in the south-west lead (the dive), two pressure ridges, two
# buried treasures. (Icicles checked 10-24: none left on the cages; the cages now sit on the floes.)
call fz_mount x=34 z=50 h=26 r=7
call ar_plants_snowy x=34 z=50 r=24 seed=12231
call icerock x=27 z=38 s=3 yaw=20 al=bergice
call icerock x=43 z=40 s=3 yaw=110 al=bergice
call icerock x=25 z=56 s=2.5 yaw=200 al=bergice
call icerock x=45 z=60 s=2.5 yaw=300 al=bergice
call icetint al=bergice
call fz_cairn x=34 z=50 al=lookout chest=lookoutchest zal=lookzone zid=berg_top msg="Ivar's cairn on the berg's top. All five floes below you - and the Kittiwake, crushed between them."
call fz_zone x=28 z=26 al=bergfoot id=berg_foot r=6 msg="The grounded iceberg. It came in with the spring ice and never left; somebody built a lookout on its top."
# the bear den (W): its mouth to the floes, the lookout's tally inside, its bear outside
call ar_cave x=-62 z=-24 h=2 yaw=0 al=bearden chest=denchest
place Note_Paper tally at -61.2 -18.6 h=2.5 drop yaw=200
place Zone_Trigger denzone at -62 -19 h=3.4
prop denzone zone.id=bear_den
prop denzone zone.radius=3
prop denzone zone.message=The bear den. Bones, a torn sealskin - and a wooden tally board the bear dragged in.
place Creature_PolarBear denbear at -56 -2 ground
prop denbear creature.count=1
prop denbear creature.respawn=0
# the sealers' hut (SE): a roofless ruin, their chest in its corner
call ar_ruin x=46 z=-44 h=2 yaw=0 al=sealhut
place Note_Paper hutlog at 45.25 -44 h=3.07 drop yaw=10
place Loot_ChestSmall hutchest at 47.3 -42.9 h=2.05 sit yaw=200
# the sister boat (SW lead): 12 m down, her chest at her side, an air pocket
call fz_dive x=-40 z=-52 d=12 r=12 yaw=0 obj=BoatStranded al=sisterboat chest=sisterchest aid=sisterair aal=sisterairz abub=sisterairb cx=6 cz=2 ax=-6 az=-3
call fz_zone x=-30 z=-38 al=leadview id=sister_lead r=6 msg="Under the black water of the lead: a second boat, the Kittiwake's sister, sunk to the bottom."
# two pressure ridges (NW, E) and their snow
call ar_ridge x1=-72 z1=30 x2=-48 z2=56 h=5 top=5 r=7
call ar_plants_snowy x=-60 z=43 r=18 seed=12234
call ar_ridge x1=62 z1=-12 x2=70 z2=20 h=5 top=4 r=6
call ar_plants_snowy x=66 z=4 r=14 seed=12237
call treasure x=-20 z=62 r=10 n=1 seed=12241
call treasure x=62 z=-24 r=8 n=1 seed=12242

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest -----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=The Floelane
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Five ice floes in the white sea, black leads between them, a sealing boat crushed between the floes - and her crew locked in cages on the ice. A winch hauls loose ice into the lead. The second island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||Floes as far as the eye goes - and on them, three cages. Somebody waves from one of them.

story sealkey|Cage key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|One of the sealers' three cage keys, from the locker on the west floe.
story rescued|The sealers freed|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The three sealers are out of their cages, and the hull bell has called them home.

note distresscard Sealer's distress card | MV KITTIWAKE - SEALER - DISTRESS\n\nIced in and crushed on the Floelane. Two crew aboard, and the relay man Ivo, who came to us off the stack with his headphones still round his neck.\nWe have no set. The courier took it "for repair" and left us a paper telling us to be quiet. Quiet! On a floe, with bears.\nBears on the floes every night: I have locked the three of them in the sealing cages for safety and taken the dinghy for help. Do not laugh, Ivo. You will thank me when you still have legs.\nCage keys in my locker on the west floe.\nThe lead to the hull opens and shuts with the ice - the winch hauls the loose floes in. Be quick about it.\n\n- Master Halvorsen
note leadsign Winch | HAUL ICE INTO LEAD\nIt holds less than a minute.
note sealerslocker Sealer's locker | Halvorsen's locker: three cage keys on a ring, an empty flask.
note engineroom Engine room | The engine room, half under the ice: the motor wheel's plans, oiled.
note wheelhouse Wheelhouse locker | The wheelhouse locker: the steering plans, a chart marked "steam harbour".
note thanks Survivors' thanks | (pinned to the bell rope, three hands taking turns)\n\nYou came for us. Thank you. Sigrid wants it written that she was not crying, it was the wind.\nThe master never came back. The dinghy has gone under, we think. He locked us up to keep the bears off and went out alone on the black water. That was Halvorsen. Stubborn to the end, and right.\nWe're going to the steam harbour, the three of us. It's warm there, they have a bath you could boil an egg in, and somebody there will have heard the Whale.\nIvo says: whoever is sending from the north is still sending. The silence is an order, he says, not a law of nature.\nGo there. 800 on the set.\n\n- Sigrid, Bo, and Ivo Rask of the relay
note silenceposter SILENCE ORDER | (a printed sheet nailed to the Kittiwake's mast, spat on)\n\nSILENCE ORDER - BY THE WARDEN OF THE COLDHOLD\n\nTo every boat, station and town of the north.\nA signal moves in the south. It is slow and it is patient, and it listens for us. Every voice on the air draws it nearer to every one of us.\nFrom this day: no transmission on any band. Sets are to be handed to the courier for safekeeping. Calls from the north are to go unanswered, whatever they say. A voice that begs is still a voice.\nThose who keep the silence will be kept. There is room below the ice.\n\nANSEL HOLT, WARDEN\n\n(Under it, scratched with a knife: "Room for who, Ansel?")
note qslcard A QSL card | (a postcard tucked behind the Kittiwake's wheel, a cartoon penguin in headphones on it)\n\nQSL - CONFIRMING OUR CONTACT\nTo: MV Kittiwake. From: SAGA DRIFT, Tor Hallen, "Sparks". Band 500, seven o'clock, signal fair, crew singing.\n\nKittiwake! Thank you for calling GOOD MORNING, ICE! to report a seal "the size of a church". Our studio expert (me) rates it a large seal. Your cook's song about it has been played four times by request (my request).\nCaller 41 was a penguin again. Said nothing. Still the best caller this week.\nKeep your set warm and your lines open. A sea with nobody talking on it is just water.\n- Sparks, 73
loot sealerslocker story:sealkey*3;Rope*2;Wool*1
prop sealerslocker loot.refill=0
loot engineroom Blueprint_MotorWheel*1;Scrap*4;Bolt*2
prop engineroom loot.refill=0
loot wheelhouse Blueprint_SteeringWheel*1;Plank*6;Nail*10
prop wheelhouse loot.refill=0

# --- DEEP 10-24: the berg, the den, the hut, the sister boat ---
story wheelkey|Wheelhouse key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The Kittiwake's wheelhouse key, frozen into the lookout on the iceberg.
note tally Lookout's tally | (a tally board, scored with a knife, dragged into the den)\n\nSEALS SIGHTED: IIII IIII III\nBEARS: IIII\nTHE WHALE'S HORN: III\nA WOMAN ON 700 BEFORE THE SET WENT: IIII IIII\n\nOn the back: She reads the ice like a weather forecast. "Lead open at the north floe, two hours. Pressure ridge east, keep off." She has been right every single time. Whoever she is, she is out there helping strangers with a hand key and no permission.\nTook the wheelhouse key up the berg with me - the master wants nobody steering while he's gone. Hung it in the lookout chest at the top. The bear has been about. If I'm late back, I'm late.\n- Ivar
note lookoutchest Sealers' lookout chest | Ivar's chest by the cairn: a glassless spyglass, the wheelhouse key.
loot lookoutchest story:wheelkey*1;Rope*2;MetalIngot*2
prop lookoutchest loot.refill=0
note denchest Bear den cache | What the bear dragged into its den: a sealer's bag, still shut.
loot denchest Leather*3;Wool*2;Raw_GenericMeat*2
prop denchest loot.refill=0
note hutlog Sealers' hut log | SEALERS' HUT - LOG (Halvorsen)\n\nThe roof went in the first storm. We sleep on the boat now, which Bo says is a step up, and Bo has seen my boat.\nIvar keeps the lookout on the berg; there is no ladder, only the slope, and he goes up it like a goat. Halvorsen keeps the keys - I write my own name like it's somebody else's, that's how tired I am.\nThe sister boat went down in the south lead in the autumn, her strongbox with her and the season's pay in it. Twelve metres. Somebody braver than me could swim for it.\nThe courier's sledge has been past twice this month, at night, without bells the second time. Odd. He always rang them for the dogs.
note hutchest Sealers' chest | Skins, hooks and a bag of nails in the hut's corner.
loot hutchest Leather*2;Nail*10;Rope*2
prop hutchest loot.refill=0
note sisterchest Sister boat's strongbox | The sister boat's strongbox, twelve metres down: the season's pay.
loot sisterchest MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Bolt*3
prop treasure12241 treasure.loot=MetalOre*3;Wool*2
prop treasure12242 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*1;CopperOre*2
prop wheelhouse if.open=has|story:wheelkey|1
prop wheelhouse else.open=message||Locked. Sigrid calls from the ice: "Ivar had the key - he kept the lookout on the berg!"

prop firstzone zone.id=first_floe
prop firstzone zone.radius=7
prop firstzone zone.message=The first floe. The ice groans under your feet.
prop hullzone zone.id=hull
prop hullzone zone.radius=6
prop hullzone zone.message=The hull floe. The Kittiwake lies crushed in front of you, her ladder still hanging down.

prop winch obj.name=winch
prop winch beh.use=Haul the loose ice into the lead
prop winch on.use=message||The winch clanks - loose floes grind into the lead. Quick: it won't hold long.\nshow|icebridge\nwait|40\nhide|icebridge\nmessage||The ice drifts apart again. The lead is open water.

prop cage1 obj.name=cage1
prop cage1 survivor.name=Sigrid
prop cage1 survivor.id=frozen_sigrid
prop cage1 survivor.key=sealkey
prop cage1 survivor.signal=cage1
prop cage1 survivor.line=At last! The bears circled us all night. Ring the hull bell when the others are out - that's our signal.
prop cage2 obj.name=cage2
prop cage2 survivor.name=Ivo
prop cage2 survivor.id=frozen_ivo
prop cage2 survivor.key=sealkey
prop cage2 survivor.signal=cage2
prop cage2 survivor.line=My hands - I can't feel my hands. Thank you. Ivo Rask, from the relay. Is Sigrid out? And Bo? Did you hear her too - the woman on 700?
prop cage3 obj.name=cage3
prop cage3 survivor.name=Bo
prop cage3 survivor.id=frozen_bo
prop cage3 survivor.key=sealkey
prop cage3 survivor.signal=cage3
prop cage3 survivor.line=Out! Out! Ring the bell, ring it - the steam harbour will hear it, they always said so.

prop hullbell obj.name=hullbell
prop hullbell beh.use=Ring the hull bell
prop hullbell if.use=signal|cage1\nsignal|cage2\nsignal|cage3\n!signal|rescued
prop hullbell on.use=message||The bell's voice rolls out over the floes. Three sealers, free, wave from the ice.\nsignal||rescued\ngive||story:rescued*1\nshow|thanks
prop hullbell else.use=message||Not yet - the bell is the crew's signal, and some of them are still in their cages.
prop thanks obj.name=thanks
prop puffers creature.count=3

quest title=The White Sea
quest intro=Floes, leads, a crushed boat - and three cages on the ice. Land on the first floe.
step reach|first_floe|1|Land on the first floe
step read|Sealer's distress card|1|Read the sealer's distress card
step reach|hull|1|Cross the lead to the hull floe (the winch hauls the ice in)
step blueprint|Blueprint_MotorWheel|1|Take the motor wheel's plans from the boat's engine room
step read|SILENCE ORDER|1|Read the paper nailed to the Kittiwake's mast
step collect|story:rescued|1|Free the three sealers (keys in the locker on the west floe) and ring the hull bell
step reach|berg_foot|1|The wheelhouse is locked and the key is not aboard. Cross the floes to the grounded iceberg in the north-east
step read|Lookout's tally|1|Find what the lookout left - the bear den in the west has his tally board
step reach|berg_top|1|Climb the iceberg on foot to Ivar's cairn on its top
step collect|story:wheelkey|1|Take the wheelhouse key from the lookout chest
step blueprint|Blueprint_SteeringWheel|1|Take the steering wheel's plans from the wheelhouse locker
step read|Survivors' thanks|1|Read the survivors' thanks on the bell rope
quest done=The sealers are going to the steam harbour. It is warm there, they say - band 800.
quest reward=MetalIngot*2;Rope*3;Leather*1

prop icebridge obj.name=icebridge
save The Floelane
